# Cases that compile here but ask a question the two dialects answer differently.
# One line per case: <name><tab><reason>. Names are source lines in test_utf8.c.
#
# Full case folding: Oniguruma folds across expansions, so (?i)ss matches ß and (?i)ß
# matches SS. This dialect folds simply — one code point to one code point — as Rust's
# regex and the JDK both do.
L0291	Oniguruma full case folding: (?i)ss matches ß
L0293	Oniguruma full case folding: (?i)ss matches ẞ
L0299	Oniguruma full case folding: (?i)ss matches ß
L0300	Oniguruma full case folding: (?i)ss matches ẞ
L0301	Oniguruma full case folding: (?i)ß matches ss
L0302	Oniguruma full case folding: (?i)ß matches SS
L0303	Oniguruma full case folding: (?i)[ß] matches ss
L0304	Oniguruma full case folding: (?i)[ß] matches SS
#
# Bare inline flags: Oniguruma scopes a(?i)b|c as a(?i:b|c) — the flag opens a group that
# swallows the rest of the alternation, changing which branch the 'a' belongs to. Here, as
# in Perl and the JDK, the flag runs to the end of the enclosing group without regrouping.
L0424	Oniguruma regroups a bare inline flag: a(?i)b|c is a(?i:b|c)
L0425	Oniguruma regroups a bare inline flag: a(?i)b|c is a(?i:b|c)
#
# A backreference to a group that did not participate matches empty in Oniguruma. Here it
# fails to match, as in the JDK and fancy-regex.
L0582	Oniguruma matches an unset backreference as empty
L0587	Oniguruma matches an unset backreference as empty
L0588	Oniguruma matches an unset backreference as empty
L0635	Oniguruma matches an unset backreference as empty
